WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:35.930
The play <i>Takekurabe</i> takes place at the beginning of the Meiji period in Yoshiwara.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:41.080
The main character, Midori, is a determined fourteen-year-old belle.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.210
The children of the town are split into two opposing factions.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:47.820
Even though Midori from the chief group has taken a fancy to him,

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:53.990
Ryogeji's son Shinyo, a member of the alley group, ignores her.

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.700
On the night of the summer festival, after attacking the chief group,

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.880
Choukichi tells Midori that Shinyo is his ally,

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.250
which transforms her attraction into anger.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:12.190
One rainy night, a young man brings flowers to Midori, but when she realizes it's Shinyo,

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.980
she is unable to call out to him.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:21.190
She drops her handkerchief in front of him, but he refuses to pick it up,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.550
and even proud Midori can't hold back her tears.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.390
A short time later, Midori bids farewell to her childhood.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:38.120
One day, Midori finds an arrangement of daffodils placed in her front door,

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.780
and she stares at them for a long time.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:46.680
That was the day that Shinyo set out to become a monk.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.660
Episode 9 - The New Midori

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.660
Maya, your feet are angled all wrong. Do it again.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:56.180
Yes, ma'am!

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:59.430
"Oh, that would be extraordinarily good fun!"

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.210
You need to turn your head at that point!

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:05.320
Is it true that the Ondine Troupe is also performing <i>Takekurabe</i>?

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:06.810
What?

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.370
They say that Ayumi Himekawa will be playing Midori.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.920
Other troupes are free to do as they please... as are we.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:20.010
Right! I need the townspeople to enter from stage right!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.260
Ayumi is playing Midori...

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.400
Why? Why would they perform the same play?

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.590
This is Masumi Hayami's little ploy to give the Daito Troupe an advantage.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:32.080
Can we really win this competition?

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.300
We <i>must</i> win this... or our troupe is finished.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.250
"I can purchase matching balls for you to play with..."

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.680
"Or I can escort you to the merchant's stall and you can choose whatever toy you desire."

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.880
"Midori, you are positively wonderful!"

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.890
She's the perfect Midori.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:55.130
We'll squash the Tsukikage Acting Troupe like the worms they are!

00:03:55.590 --> 00:04:01.130
I hear the girl who played Beth is also playing Midori. Maya Kitajima, I mean.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.010
<i>That</i> girl...

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.580
"How does this concern San in the slightest?!"

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:09.380
"If you wish to brawl with Shouta..."

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.410
Your lips should literally shake with anger at this point!

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:12.860
Y-Yes!

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.120
"How does this concern San in the slightest?!"

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.680
Midori can't control her anger!

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.850
"San never ran! He never hid Shouta!"

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:24.770
"Do you see Shouta anywhere?!"

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:34.190
They got hideously drunk and had the urge to beat Sangoro to a pulp without provocation!

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:39.210
Midori's anger is reaching its boiling point and she can't keep it in!

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.000
"How does this concern San in the slightest?!"

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:46.120
"How does this concern San in the slightest?!"

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.700
"How does this concern San in the slightest?!"

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.340
She's pushing her too hard.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:52.990
Look at her hand!

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.970
I want you to show more anger!

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:58.960
Your friend has been attacked for no reason!

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.250
You can't control your anger!

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.470
You can't take it! You can't take it!

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.600
You're so angry! You're so angry!

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:09.000
Your rage rises from the very pit of your stomach!

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:17.170
"How does this concern San in the slightest?!"

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:22.880
"How does this concern San in the slightest?!"

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:26.880
"San never ran! He never hid Shouta!"

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.720
"Do you see Shouta anywhere?!"

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.310
Where's the brush seller?

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:31.930
Here!

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.650
"Stop, Midori!"

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:35.610
"Take your hands off me!"

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:36.390
"You disgust me!"

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:41.120
"If you want to hit someone, then hit me!"

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:44.340
"I'll face you!"

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:48.510
Stop right there.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:52.580
Make sure you remember your breathing, your intensity.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:06:00.940
Miss, I... well, when you were hitting me... for a moment, I...

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:07.850
I really hated you for a moment and then, my voice and body reflected that.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:11.600
I will give it my best shot!

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:14.220
What a strange child.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.820
But from this point on, Maya...

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:22.000
you'll have to make the hardest and most painful sacrifices.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:31.860
I wonder if the person who gave me the purple roses will come and watch us again.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:37.840
Whoever he or she is... they're my only fan in the world.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:42.360
I'll do my best... for their sake as well.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:45.530
Welcome back, Master Masumi.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:52.610
Your father would like to hear your business report for the day.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:55.000
All right. I will change and come down immediately.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:55.880
Yes, sir.

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:07.880
Work, work, work. My only common ground with my father is through work.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.920
Masumi... come back!

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.920
Masumi, you shouldn't disobey your father.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:43.940
If you remember that, you can become part of this family.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.160
Mother.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.190
I've been fine with it up until now.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:00.520
So why can't I abide it anymore?

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:05.300
Just once, I'd like to live my life freely,

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.270
even if I end up in the gutter because of it.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:11.510
That girl is trying her utmost to follow her own path.

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:14.310
She tries so hard.... it's almost heartbreaking.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.420
Maya! Your expression is completely wrong!

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.200
In her heart of hearts, Midori <i>loves</i> Shinyo!

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.000
Even though she drags him through the mud, she can't help how she feels for him.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:27.680
Consider that! You need to consider Midori's feelings!

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.250
I'm sorry.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:34.760
Your eyes need to convey more sorrow!

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.760
Try to pretend someone <i>you</i> care about, even if only a little bit, is standing in front of you.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:54.720
Hey, Maya!

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:56.920
"I wish we could see each other..."

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:59.310
There! That's the look.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.880
We'll end here for today.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.430
Thanks.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.440
Thank you.

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:08.980
Is something wrong, Ms. Tsukikage?

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.650
Everyone's progressing so well.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.760
Kitajima too...

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:15.400
Yes. She's portraying everything exactly as I tell her to.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.660
But it's not enough.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.290
There's something missing.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:24.170
To prepare for the Tokyo District Preliminaries, each participating troupe...

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:28.470
is allowed to use the venue of the performance only once before the competition.

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:32.190
The Tsukikage Acting Troupe also have an appointed day.

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.750
What are you saying?

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.850
The representative who contacted us told us our allotted time was today at 6:30pm.

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:41.130
Well, it says here that the Tsukikage Acting Troupe was moved...

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.010
to Wednesday last week.

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:47.320
Are you trying to tell me that we're expected to perform without even using the stage first?!

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.680
It's impossible to put on a play without getting a feel...

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:52.600
for the dimensions of the stage and coordinating the lighting!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:55.920
Hurry up! The Ondine Troupe is about to go on!

00:09:57.010 --> 00:10:00.760
Well, why don't you ask Mr. Onodera from the Ondine Troupe?

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:04.490
He's on the committee for the stage schedule.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:07.690
Onodera's a member of the committee?

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:10.260
Excuse me!

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.600
"Stop it, Shouta! Stop everyone!"

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.320
"We were having such a pleasant time together!"

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.510
Her voice projects so beautifully.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:24.340
She sparkles just by being present on stage.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.050
She's so different...

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.850
Her Midori is completely different from mine.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.930
Mine doesn't even compete with hers.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.980
Every single gesture she makes appears animated.

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:38.890
The way she moves... the expressions on her face...

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:44.180
That right there... that's the Midori of <i>Takekurabe</i>.

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:47.960
"Let's try to get along and play dice instead."

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.490
"Auntie... I'm here to buy a brush!"

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:54.310
Sakurakouji is playing Shinyo...

00:10:54.780 --> 00:11:00.790
"Really? Promise me you'll bring me the most beautiful daffodil when spring arrives!"

00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:03.350
"I promise."

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.300
"Oh, it fills me with joy!"

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:08.600
She's just like you'd expect: her Midori is perfect.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.070
To be brutally honest, Maya's at a disadvantage.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:14.350
"This is for the brush."

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:16.050
"Shin!"

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:30.320
There are amateurs and then there are pros.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:34.080
Yeah. The others are good, but Midori is on a whole different level.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.470
Maya, our rehearsal is about to start.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:40.780
I can't go.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:42.130
Maya...

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:45.640
What's the point? No matter what I do, I can never be as good as Ayumi.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.840
Maya, no one else can do it.

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.560
I said I don't want to... I don't want to!

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.880
I can't... I just can't!

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:56.060
You want to surrender before we've even put up a fight?

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.920
Yes! That's what I said!

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:01.470
I already know that Ayumi is more talented and better at acting than I am,

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:04.070
so there's nothing I can do!

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.900
If you hate acting so much, then I'm taking the role of Midori away from you!

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:18.970
You're an embarrassment!

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:23.750
You'll stay in here until we're done with our rehearsals!

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:29.220
But ma'am! Ma'am! Ma'am!

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:32.810
Ma'am...

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:35.290
Ma'am...

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:45.050
I have no talent! I never want to act again!

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.380
There! I said it!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:04.000
Why are there people like Ayumi Himekawa?

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.800
She's pretty, smart and from a wealthy family.

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:12.350
Why couldn't I be born with those things?

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:16.420
Mom... I want to come home.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:18.630
I want to come back to you.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:34.560
Sayaka!

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:35.790
Your breakfast.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.970
I brought you a blanket and a flashlight too.

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:38.910
Thank you.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:44.670
Ms. Tsukikage is always harsher to me than anyone else.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.160
I envy you.

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:51.640
She has such high expectations of you.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:54.070
She has some kind of plan for you.

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:57.440
She has expectations of me?

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:14.470
Everyone's working so hard, even late at night.

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:24.880
"I can purchase matching balls for you to play with..."

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:28.930
"Or I can escort you to the merchant's stall and you can choose whatever toy you desire."

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:31.120
"What shall we do then?"

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.930
"Everything is more exciting when there's a crowd!"

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:35.340
"We'll form some kind of plan!"

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:38.200
This feels so different from our rehearsals...

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:41.350
The lines are flowing so naturally...

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.330
When I recited the lines before, Midori sounded so pretentious...

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.590
The lines are exactly the same,

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:50.370
but Midori's personality now feels completely different.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.260
The way she moves...

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:57.840
You can depict so many different personalities by just changing the way she moves.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:01.450
That's it! You create the role.

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:03.730
Why didn't I realize that before?

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:07.510
Just by changing the tone of my voice or the way I look at something...

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.790
I can become a bright young girl from the town.

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:13.990
Then, let's create this role!

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.370
I have my own Midori mask.

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.240
My own Midori.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:28.100
"Oh Shouta! Say something."

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:31.330
"Look at you! You're blushing!"

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:32.880
"Say something."

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.560
"Come on, say something."

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:46.400
"Oh Shouta! Say something."

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:47.780
"Say something."

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.150
"I'm not blushing at all."

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.900
"You shouldn't tease me so, Miss Midori."

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:56.620
Well? What's the next line?

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:57.850
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.680
Please let me out!

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:04.180
When are you going to let me out?

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:07.330
When you're able to surpass Ayumi's Midori.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.530
Surpass... Ayumi?

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:13.860
It's possible for me to surpass someone like Ayumi?

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.830
Yes, there's a way.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:18.520
Then, please tell me!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:21.930
What can I do to create a better Midori than Ayumi!

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:25.830
I won't deny that Miss Ayumi has some wonderful qualities.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:29.400
She was born into acting, so her depiction of Midori will undoubtedly be perfect.

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:34.600
But the more perfect she is, the more trapped she will become...

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:36.260
in the author's version of Midori.

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.170
The author's version of Midori?

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:44.030
Yes. That's your only hope to beat her.

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:46.980
You need to depict a Midori that's a complete contrast...

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:49.280
to what they'll be expecting.

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:51.690
You need to create an entirely new Midori!

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.500
A new Midori?

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:58.370
And when you have perfected that, you will make a much stronger impression on the audience...

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.080
than a perfect but lifeless Midori.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:05.000
That will give you the possibility to surpass her.

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:10.750
I'll do it! No matter what it takes!

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.240
Very well.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:14.270
This door will separate us, inside and out.

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:17.990
Do you advance or do you let me advance on you? This is a battle.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:21.720
If you lose, I want you to give up acting and leave this place forever!

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:25.670
But if I lose, I shall give you another chance to play Midori.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.240
Begin!

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.730
"Listen to you... you're angry again."

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.210
Now, with more anger.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.480
"<i>Listen</i> to you... you're angry again!"

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:34.740
Now, as though you're mocking him.

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:36.920
"Listen to you... you're <i>angry</i> again."

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:40.930
That's pretty good... now, say it while laughing!

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:44.310
"Listen to you... you're angry again!"

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:46.510
Now, it troubles you...

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:48.900
"Listen to you... you're angry again!"

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:51.090
Mock him again.

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:53.300
"Listen to you... you're <i>angry</i> again!"

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.280
Softer!

00:17:58.320 --> 00:17:59.400
Soft laughter!

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:02.840
Let's leave this scene.

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:03.890
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:06.510
Let's try the scene where you break up the fight.

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:12.760
Ma'am... Ma'am!

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:17.000
I'm fine... carry on!

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:25.340
"That's what I said. Stop it! Stop, Shouta... everyone else too!"

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:26.910
Make your tone edgier.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.980
"That's what I said. Stop it! Stop, Shouta... everyone else too!"

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:32.050
Now... angrier!

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:38.070
So she locked Maya in there so she could calm down and take an inward look at herself.

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:40.890
If locked up by herself in a cold room, bored and with nothing else to do,

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.640
she knew she'd start acting again.

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:47.760
Those two... kinda scare me.

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:49.140
Now, the next line...

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:53.350
It grew dark, then light, then dark again.

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:55.870
Their one-on-one tutorial continued,

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:59.950
two passionate spirits clashing against one other.

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:04.380
"Shin, you can wipe the mud off with this..."

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.430
Now, say it like you can't bear it!

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:08.730
What's the matter?!

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:10.720
Nothing...

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.090
"Shin, you can wipe the mud off with this..."

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:14.530
Now, kinder...

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:16.780
Now, more confused...

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:20.050
Now more sympathetic, as though from the bottom of your heart...

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:25.080
That's it! That's good.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.720
She's starting to grasp it.

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:30.750
Her new Midori.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:34.710
Ma'am...

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.680
Do it again...

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:38.140
"Silence!"

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:40.090
More violent!

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:41.350
"<i>Silence</i>!"

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:42.890
Now, try to hide your impatience...

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:44.630
"Silence!"

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:54.040
Leave me alone...

00:19:54.820 --> 00:20:01.190
The new Midori is about to be born!

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:04.040
"What's the matter, Midori?"

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.570
"No..."

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:10.190
"Mother... these daffodils by the front door..."

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.510
At last!

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:15.200
Ma'am!

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:19.240
"Who could have left my favorites for me?

00:20:19.240 --> 00:20:23.760
"I feel... I feel like a kid again.."

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:28.480
"Why do I feel it in the very bottom of my heart?"

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:30.060
Stop there.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.060
Stop right there.

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:36.460
You gaze at the daffodils. You gently close your eyes.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:41.880
Don't move a muscle!

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:46.270
Quietly... Just freeze... silently....

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:51.600
And then, from stage right... the voices of people filter in...

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:56.250
The light slowly fades as if embracing Midori...

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:58.250
Then, the curtain...

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:00.750
Ma'am! Ma'am!

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:05.980
She'll be fine. She just fainted.

00:21:07.710 --> 00:21:09.380
Please take this.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.190
Maya... Maya!

00:21:22.190 --> 00:21:23.600
Say something!

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:31.080
She's passed out.

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:33.880
Well, they've been sparring for five whole days!

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:37.420
But look, she's smiling.

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:43.760
All this took place a week before the Japanese National Acting Competition was due to begin.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:48.610
Will Maya be able to best Ayumi?

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
Gomennette iwaretara

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.930
When you say "I'm sorry,"

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
Anata wo semerarenai yo

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:10.670
I can't blame you.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
Sonna watashi wo kitto shitterundeshou

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:21.510
I'm sure you know that's how I am.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
Nee zurui yo

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:25.810
That's not fair.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Yasashisa ni damasaretatte

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:33.620
Even if I'm being fooled by kindness,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
Anata nara isso iito shinjita

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:44.210
I believed that with you, it might be worth it.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Sayonara wa doushite itoshiindarou

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:53.690
Why are goodbyes so precious,

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
Hanareteyuku noni

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:58.250
even though they mean we're separating?

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
Ushinatta ondo wo oboeteruyo

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:07.640
I remember how it got colder.

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
Yurushitai dakara anata

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:13.500
I want to forgive you, so please don't go.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Ikanaide douka ikanaide

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:21.410
Whatever you do... just don't go.

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:26.580
The main character in <i>Takekurabe</i> is a girl named Midori who lives in Yoshiwara.

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:29.660
The boy she loves has chosen to become a monk.

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:32.860
Miss Kitajima, you are practically an amateur.

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:36.040
Do you honestly think you can depict the depth of Midori's feelings,

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:38.520
her anger and her sadness, better than I can?

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:41.610
I'm sorry to have to tell you this, but it looks like the Tsukikage Acting Troupe's fate...

00:23:41.610 --> 00:23:43.680
has already been decided.

00:23:43.680 --> 00:23:46.350
What's with this silence?

00:23:46.640 --> 00:23:50.820
What's happening on Maya's stage?!

00:23:46.830 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 10 - The Two Midoris of <i>Takekurabe</i>
